==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|criticise||UK}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krey-}}
{{suffix|en|critic|ize}}; first element from {{der|en|grc|κριτικός||of or for judging, able to discern}}, from {{m|grc|κρίσις||crisis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹɪtɪsaɪz/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|crit|i|cize}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|ambitransitive}}

# To [[find fault]] (with something).
#: {{syn|en|censure|pick at|Thesaurus:criticize}}
#: {{hypo|en|find fault|shoot down|run down|trash out|fustigate|drub|excoriate}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''criticized''' him for endangering people's lives.}}
# To [[evaluate]] (something), [[assess]]ing its [[merit]]s and [[fault]]s.
#: {{syn|en|censure|appraise|judge}}

